==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|cochlea||snail}}, from {{der|en|grc|κοχλίας||spiral, snail shell}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkɒk.lɪə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|cochleae}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The complex, spirally coiled, tapered [[cavity]] of the [[inner ear]] in which sound vibrations are converted into nerve impulses.
# A spiral-shaped [[shell]], especially that of a [[snail]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|cochlear}}

